# Normalize to LF in the repository, accept CRLF on checkout on Windows.
#
# Why this matters here specifically:
#   * .ps1 files must be readable as ANSI by Windows PowerShell 5.1 when they
#     are BOM-free. LF endings avoid the mixed-ending class of bug.
#   * Skill SKILL.md frontmatter is parsed by YAML readers that are sensitive
#     to a BOM and to mixed line endings. Both are prevented here.
#   * A BOM is the real hazard and it is banned below rather than normalized:
#     `utf8` in PowerShell 5.1 emits one.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never a BOM. YAML frontmatter and JSON5 configs both break on one.
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonc text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Shell and batch scripts: CRLF is required for .cmd on Windows.
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# .ps1 content must stay ASCII (PS 5.1 reads a BOM-less file as ANSI).
# Enforced by tools/gate.py - not via working-tree-encoding, which silently
# transcodes and would hide the problem instead of reporting it.
# Binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.rdc  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
*.sys  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary

# Never mangle these even if a heuristic thinks they are text.
collections.lock.json -diff
package-lock.json -diff
